TOPOLOGY FOUNDATIONS (order-induced)

  Order topology (on a total order)
    subbasis:  { x | x < a }  and  { x | a < x }
    on ℝ this recovers the usual topology
    connected ⇔ Dedekind-complete (no gaps)
    compact ⇔ complete + bounded (extreme-value theorem)

  Alexandrov topology (on any preorder)
    open sets = upper sets
    (U open and x ∈ U, x ≤ y  ⇒  y ∈ U)
    finest topology whose specialization preorder
    recovers the original order

  Specialization preorder of a topology
    x ≤ y  ⇔  x ∈ cl{y}
    (or every open containing x contains y)
    T₀  ⇔  antisymmetric specialization
    T₁  ⇔  specialization is equality (discrete order)

  Scott topology (on a dcpo / complete lattice)
    open sets are upper sets inaccessible by directed sups
    used in domain theory and denotational semantics

  Lower / upper topology
    subbasis of principal down-sets or up-sets
    coarser than order / Alexandrov topologies

  Links
    lattices of open sets          → frames / locales
    continuous lattices            → injective spaces
    well-orders                    → discrete / successor topology
    dense total orders             → no isolated points
